.Dd May 28, 2026
.Dt CAP_RT_SYSTEM 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm cap_rt_system
.Nd CAP_RT system operation gating
.Sh SYNOPSIS
To load at boot:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
echo 'cap_rt_system_load="YES"' >> /boot/loader.conf
.Ed
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
service gates privileged system operations via MACF hooks.
Once an operation is claimed, all processes are denied except
those with the claimer's nonce or an authorized token.
Even root cannot bypass the MACF enforcement.
.Pp
Operations are claimed by bitmask.
Multiple operations can be claimed in a single call.
.Ss Gated Operations
.Bl -tag -width "SYS_GATE_KLDUNLOAD"
.It Dv SYS_GATE_KLDLOAD
Kernel module loading via
.Xr kldload 2 .
.It Dv SYS_GATE_KLDUNLOAD
Kernel module unloading via
.Xr kldunload 2 .
.It Dv SYS_GATE_KLDSTAT
Kernel module enumeration via
.Xr kldstat 2 .
.It Dv SYS_GATE_REBOOT
System reboot via
.Xr reboot 2 .
.It Dv SYS_GATE_SWAPON
Adding swap devices via
.Xr swapon 2 .
.It Dv SYS_GATE_SWAPOFF
Removing swap devices via
.Xr swapoff 2 .
.It Dv SYS_GATE_SYSCTL
Security-relevant
.Xr sysctl 3
writes.
Read operations are not gated.
.It Dv SYS_GATE_KENV
Kernel environment modification via
.Xr kenv 2
(set and unset only; get and dump are not gated).
.It Dv SYS_GATE_ACCT
Process accounting control via
.Xr acct 2 .
.El
.Ss Protocol
The service is accessed via
.Dv CAP_RT_CALL
on an instance fd obtained from
.Dv CAP_RT_CONNECT
with the service name
.Dq system .
.Pp
Requests use
.Vt struct sys_request
with an operation code and a gates bitmask:
.Bl -tag -width "SYS_OP_AUTHORIZE"
.It Dv SYS_OP_CLAIM
Claim the specified gates.
The caller's nonce becomes the owner.
.It Dv SYS_OP_RELEASE
Release the claim.
.It Dv SYS_OP_MINT
Create an access token fd (returned as a reply fd).
Only the claim owner can mint tokens.
.It Dv SYS_OP_AUTHORIZE
Called on a token fd.
Adds the caller's nonce to the authorized set.
Authorization persists while the token fd is open.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kldload 2 ,
.Xr reboot 2 ,
.Xr sysctl 3 ,
.Xr cap_rt 4 ,
.Xr oracled 8
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
first appeared in 5BSD.
